IMPORT prelude

-- Manufacture of Optical Discs Act 2004 (Singapore) -- what counts as an optical disc (s 2, The Schedule), the need for a licence and
-- for licensed premises (ss 4, 5), grounds for refusal, suspension and cancellation (ss 7(2), 10(1)), when a suspension, surrender
-- or appeal takes effect or is in time (ss 10(3), 11(2), 14(1)), the duty to mark the manufacturer's code and the false-code offence
-- (ss 15, 17), the penalties (ss 19(3), 20(3), 22, 23, 24), liability of officers and partners (s 25), forfeiture (s 21) and
-- composition (s 26).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MODA2004.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021"; the latest amendment annotated in
-- the body is [3/2013; 9/2018] on s 20. The deposit's metadata records it as the current version as at 1 October 2026.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0085 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper
-- question yet. The Act is short (31 sections), so this row takes nearly all of what a manufacturer, its officers or anyone
-- dealing with an officer meets. Not encoded: appointments (s 3), application procedure (s 6), form and duration of licences (s 8),
-- variation of conditions (s 9, beyond noting it needs notice), the register (s 12), the content of records (s 13, which is
-- prescribed), marking standards (s 16), arrest, inspection and computer-search powers (ss 18 to 20) except the offences they
-- create, protection from liability (s 27), District Court jurisdiction (s 28), exemption, Schedule amendment and regulations
-- (ss 29 to 31, beyond a flag for an exemption). No regulations were retrieved, so nothing prescribed is known: which offences are
-- compoundable, the record contents, the marking standards and any further suspension grounds under s 10(1)(d).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Manufacture of Optical Discs Act 2004 -- licensing, marking and penalties`

§§ `2 and The Schedule -- what is an optical disc`

-- s 2: "optical disc" means "any medium or article specified in the Schedule". The Schedule: "1. Compact discs (CD), including
-- compact discs-read only memory (CD-ROM). 2. Digital video discs (DVD), including digital video discs-read only memory (DVD-ROM).
-- 3. Video compact discs (VCD). 4. Master discs. 5. Stampers."
-- Nothing else is listed: a Blu-ray disc is not in the Schedule, and the Minister may add to it only by order in the Gazette (s 30).
DECLARE Medium IS ONE OF
    `a compact disc`
    `a CD-ROM`
    `a DVD`
    `a DVD-ROM`
    `a video compact disc`
    `a master disc`
    `a stamper`
    `a Blu-ray disc`
    `a USB flash drive`
    `a vinyl record`

GIVEN `the medium` IS A Medium
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the medium is an optical disc` IF
    CONSIDER `the medium`
    WHEN `a Blu-ray disc` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a USB flash drive` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a vinyl record` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `4 and 5 -- licence and licensed premises`

-- s 4(1): "a person must not engage in the manufacture for sale or other commercial purpose of any optical disc in any place except
-- under the authority, and in accordance with the terms and conditions, of a licence." (2) offence.
-- (3): "any person who owns, directs, manages or otherwise has control of a business which undertakes the manufacture of optical
-- discs is deemed to engage in the manufacture of optical discs for a commercial purpose."
-- s 2: "manufacture" means "the processes and activities involved in the making of optical discs, including (where applicable)
-- mastering or replicating or both".
-- s 29: the Minister may by order exempt any person or class of persons from all or any provisions.
GIVEN `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owns, directs, manages or controls a disc-making business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person engages in commercial manufacture` IF
    `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` OR `owns, directs, manages or controls a disc-making business`

GIVEN `the medium` IS A Medium,
      `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `owns, directs, manages or controls a disc-making business` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is exempted by Ministerial order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `manufacturing without a licence is an offence` IF
        `the medium is an optical disc` `the medium`
    AND `the person engages in commercial manufacture` `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` `owns, directs, manages or controls a disc-making business`
    AND (NOT `holds a licence`)
    AND (NOT `is exempted by Ministerial order`)

-- s 5: "Any licensee who manufactures for sale or other commercial purpose any optical disc in a place other than the licensed
-- premises shall be guilty of an offence."
GIVEN `is a licensee` IS A BOOLEAN, `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` IS A BOOLEAN, `at the licensed premises` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `manufacturing away from the licensed premises is an offence` IF
    `is a licensee` AND `makes discs for sale or other commercial purpose` AND (NOT `at the licensed premises`)

§§ `7(2) and 10(1) -- refusal, suspension and cancellation`

-- s 7(2): the Registrar may refuse to grant or renew if satisfied that (a) the applicant, or any individual who is or is to be "a
-- director, manager, secretary or other similar officer of the applicant, has been convicted of an offence under this Act"; (b)
-- either "has provided to the Registrar any false or misleading information"; or (c) "the applicant is, for any other reason, not a
-- fit and proper person". s 7(1) leaves a general discretion to refuse besides.
GIVEN `applicant or officer convicted under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applicant or officer gave false or misleading information` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `applicant not fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a section 7(2) refusal ground exists` IF
    `applicant or officer convicted under this Act` OR `applicant or officer gave false or misleading information` OR `applicant not fit and proper`

-- s 10(1): the Registrar may suspend or cancel if satisfied that (a) "there exists a ground on which he or she may refuse to grant or
-- renew a licence under section 7"; (b) the licensee "has contravened any term or condition of the licence or any provision of this
-- Act"; (c) "has ceased to carry on the business of manufacturing optical discs in the licensed premises"; or (d) prescribed
-- circumstances (none retrieved). (2): written notice of intention and an opportunity for written representations first.
GIVEN `a section 7 ground exists` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `licensee contravened a condition or the Act` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `licensee ceased the business at the premises` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `notice and a chance to make representations were given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may suspend or cancel` IF
        (`a section 7 ground exists` OR `licensee contravened a condition or the Act` OR `licensee ceased the business at the premises`)
    AND `notice and a chance to make representations were given`

§§ `10(3), 11(2) and 14(1) -- when things take effect`

-- s 10(3): a suspension or cancellation takes effect "(a) where there is no appeal ... on the expiry of 14 days from the date on which
-- the notice ... is served on the licensee; or (b) where there is an appeal ... when the suspension or cancellation ... is confirmed
-- by the Minister." Days are counted as day numbers. Reading "on the expiry of 14 days from" the service date as service day plus 14
-- is an inference (the Interpretation Act was not read). If the Minister varies rather than confirms, the text gives no date; this
-- encoding treats it as not having taken effect.
GIVEN `served on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `an appeal was made` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `confirmed by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `confirmed on day` IS A NUMBER,
      `today` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the suspension or cancellation is in effect` IF
    IF `an appeal was made`
    THEN `confirmed by the Minister` AND `today` AT LEAST `confirmed on day`
    ELSE `today` AT LEAST `served on day` PLUS 14

-- s 11(2): "The surrender takes effect on the date the Registrar receives the licence and the notice ... or, where a later date is
-- specified in the notice, on that later date." An earlier date specified in the notice has no effect.
GIVEN `received on day` IS A NUMBER, `day specified in the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day the surrender takes effect` MEANS
    IF `day specified in the notice` GREATER THAN `received on day` THEN `day specified in the notice` ELSE `received on day`

-- s 14(1): a person aggrieved by a decision of the Registrar under Part 2 "may appeal to the Minister within 14 days after the date on
-- which the person is notified of the decision or any longer period allowed by the Minister." (3): the Minister's decision is final.
-- `extension ends on day` is 0 where no longer period was allowed.
GIVEN `notified on day` IS A NUMBER, `appealed on day` IS A NUMBER, `extension ends on day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF
    `appealed on day` AT MOST `notified on day` PLUS 14 OR `appealed on day` AT MOST `extension ends on day`

§§ `15 and 17 -- the manufacturer's code`

-- s 15(1): every licensee must mark each optical disc it manufactures with its manufacturer's code. (2): it "need not comply ... if,
-- and only if, a person who owns or is a licensee of the right to reproduce the content in the optical disc, which the licensee has
-- verified, has requested the licensee not to mark the optical disc". (3) offence.
GIVEN `the disc was marked with the code` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `a rights holder asked for no marking` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the licensee verified the rights holder` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failing to mark is an offence` IF
    (NOT `the disc was marked with the code`) AND (NOT (`a rights holder asked for no marking` AND `the licensee verified the rights holder`))

-- s 17(1): "Any person who falsely applies, or causes to be falsely applied, to an optical disc a manufacturer's code or any mark so
-- resembling a manufacturer's code as to be calculated to deceive shall be guilty of an offence." (2): "it is a defence for the
-- person charged to prove that the person acted without intent to deceive or defraud." Any person, not only licensees.
GIVEN `applied a false or deceptively similar code` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved no intent to deceive or defraud` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `applying a false code is an offence` IF
    `applied a false or deceptively similar code` AND (NOT `proved no intent to deceive or defraud`)

§§ `19(3), 20(3), 22, 23 and 24 -- penalties`

-- s 22 (offences under Part 2 or 3: ss 4, 5, 13, 15, 17): body corporate $200,000, second or subsequent $400,000; any other case
-- $100,000 or 12 months or both, second or subsequent $200,000 or 2 years or both.
-- s 19(3) (no exemplars when required, without reasonable excuse), s 23(3) (false information, refusing to answer, failing to
-- produce) and s 24 (obstructing, impeding, assaulting or interfering with an officer): body corporate $100,000, second or subsequent
-- $200,000; any other case $50,000 or 6 months or both, second or subsequent $100,000 or 12 months or both.
-- s 20(3) (refusing technical assistance with a computer): "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 12 months or to both" -- no separate figure for a body corporate and no step-up for a repeat.
-- Imprisonment of a body corporate is shown as 0 months: the text gives it no term (an inference for s 20(3), which does not
-- distinguish).
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `manufacturing without a licence`
    `manufacturing away from the licensed premises`
    `a records failure`
    `failing to mark the code`
    `applying a false code`
    `failing to provide exemplars`
    `refusing computer assistance`
    `giving false information`
    `obstructing an officer`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence is under Part 2 or 3` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `manufacturing without a licence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `manufacturing away from the licensed premises` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a records failure` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `failing to mark the code` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `applying a false code` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `the offence` EQUALS `refusing computer assistance` THEN 20000
    ELSE IF `the offence is under Part 2 or 3` `the offence`
         THEN IF `is a body corporate`
              THEN IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 400000 ELSE 200000
              ELSE IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 200000 ELSE 100000
         ELSE IF `is a body corporate`
              THEN IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 200000 ELSE 100000
              ELSE IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 100000 ELSE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a repeat offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF `is a body corporate` THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the offence` EQUALS `refusing computer assistance` THEN 12
         ELSE IF `the offence is under Part 2 or 3` `the offence`
              THEN IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 24 ELSE 12
              ELSE IF `is a repeat offence` THEN 12 ELSE 6

§§ `21, 25 and 26 -- forfeiture, officers and composition`

-- s 21(1): on conviction "the court must, unless it is of the view that the offence is minor or that there are exceptional
-- circumstances for deciding otherwise, order the person to forfeit to the Government any optical disc, article or thing in relation
-- to which, or by means of which, the offence was committed." (2) in addition to any penalty.
GIVEN `convicted of an offence under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `the court views it as minor` IS A BOOLEAN, `exceptional circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forfeiture must be ordered` IF
    `convicted of an offence under this Act` AND (NOT `the court views it as minor`) AND (NOT `exceptional circumstances`)

-- s 25(1): where an offence by a body corporate is proved "(a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of an officer;
-- or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on his or her part, the officer as well as the body corporate shall be guilty". (3) the
-- same for a partner of a partnership; (4) for an officer or governing-body member of an unincorporated association. (5) "officer"
-- includes any director, manager, secretary "and includes any person purporting to act in any such capacity".
GIVEN `the organisation committed the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the officer consented or connived` IS A BOOLEAN, `attributable to the officer's neglect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer is also guilty` IF
    `the organisation committed the offence` AND (`the officer consented or connived` OR `attributable to the officer's neglect`)

-- s 26: the Registrar may "compound any offence under this Act which is prescribed as a compoundable offence by collecting from a
-- person reasonably suspected of having committed the offence a sum not exceeding $10,000." Which offences are prescribed is not
-- known here.
GIVEN `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `the offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `the sum` AT MOST 10000
